## Objective
- Run an autonomous bug-bounty session against `account.ui.com` per `skills/AGENT.md`, discovering UI routes/API endpoints and testing each route for client-side and server-side bugs, writing findings to `result/`.

## Important Details
- Authorized scope per `data/targets.txt`: `account.ui.com` (domain-only). Prior session deferred all cross-origin APIs (`sso.ui.com`, `sso.ubnt.com`, `*.svc.ui.com`, etc.) as out-of-scope per AGENT.md §2.2.
- **Key correction:** `creds/test-account.txt` targets `https://account.ui.com/login` (NOT console.byteplus.com). Prior session misread this.
- Two valid test accounts, both now logged in:
  - A: `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345` (UUID `d8946fad-2b8e-4cf0-82c5-5d955b57b829`, username `testttt12`)
  - B: `overrated.chinchilla337@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345` (UUID `7c5aab2b-e568-40de-a7a5-ec27df1db94b`, username `test-account-b`)
- Maildrop inboxes (external, used only to read MFA codes): `https://maildrop.cc/inbox/?mailbox=tan.tiger5564` and `.../?mailbox=overrated.chinchilla337`. MFA codes appear as `<2 letters> - <6 digits>`.
- Login flow: email step → password step → `/login/mfa` (6-digit email code) → `/login/trust-device` (chose "Not now") → `/`.
- Account A has an existing Android session from India (`session_id 951c9742-e7f0-4e5c-b162-814c3106c672`); current A session id `03616c63-b274-4db4-acbe-510fbbbf54f2`.
- CORS tested: `sso.ui.com` returns `vary: origin` and **no** `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` for `https://evil.example`, `http://localhost:8000`, `null` → CORS appears correctly restricted (not a finding).
- `PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self` with `{"role":"admin"}` → 204 but `/user/self/roles` stays `{"roles":[]}` (likely ignored field). Second write returned `429 {"error":"RATE_LIMITED"}` → writes are rate-limited; slow down.
- Bundle source base: `getBaseUrl()` uses `sso.ui.com` when host matches `\.ui\.com`.
- The 39 routes + inventory were source-mapped by the prior session; `/requests`, `/mysupport`, `/services` redirect to `/` or 404 catch-all in this account (support surface appears unavailable; 0 Zendesk tickets).
- Account data is empty across billing/eSIM/UMR/CAP/enterprise/cloudaccess (cloudaccess returns 403 "Missing Authentication Token").
- Do NOT spam writes (429). Avoid destructive changes to test accounts. Discord notification only if a confirmed vuln is found.
- Session start now: ~2026-10-30T06:30Z; MCP works on port 9222.

