## Objective
- Act as an autonomous bug-bounty agent per `skills/AGENT.md`: discover and test UI routes/API endpoints on `account.ui.com` (authorized scope in `data/targets.txt`), one route at a time with client-side then server-side testing, document findings/progress in `result/`, and notify Discord webhook on confirmed vulnerabilities.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`.
- Scope: `account.ui.com` domain-only. AGENT.md §2 forbids pivoting to sibling subdomains. Prior runs documented a "reversible interpretation" that exercising APIs the SPA actually calls (`sso.ui.com`, `account.svc.ui.com`, billing/other `*.svc.ui.com`) is required to exercise in-scope UI; this is recorded in `result/scope.md`, `result/out-of-scope.txt`, `result/unresolved.md` (U-02). Continue cautiously: only SPA-called endpoints, no enumeration of unrelated hosts.
- Target state: hash `ff311b9fcf5fa16d5c8d15bb89a4bb1f1d84e7a625dc0acb53dec02e1accd998`, `decision=preserved`; continuation session appended to `result/logs/session.md` at `2026-10-30T07:13Z`.
- Test accounts (`creds/test-account.txt`):
  - A: `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`; uuid `d8946fad-2b8e-4cf0-82c5-5d955b57b829`; username `testttt12`.
  - B: `overrated.chinchilla337@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`; uuid `7c5aab2b-e568-40de-a7a5-ec27df1db94b`; username `test-account-b`.
- MFA codes come from `https://maildrop.cc/inbox/?mailbox=<mailbox>` in the browser (format `UB - 203123`); browser-side reading is the only working method.
- Chrome DevTools MCP is live; pages: 1 = A session logged in (`https://account.ui.com/`), 2 = maildrop B inbox, 3 = B session in `isolatedContext=account-b`.
- AAL2 (`/api/sso/v1/user/self/login/level`) was `level:2` with ~401s left; re-login may be needed for AAL2-gated tests.
- Rate limiting is aggressive: `429 {"error":"RATE_LIMITED","detail":"Too many requests","retry_after":0}`; space requests ~1-5s.
- JS bundle: `assets/index-D5t7M7xo.js`, sha256 `ce9950c975a42cac66f5c2ea759d655e96c441d34df6a6b8190b09d60ea1c468`, 7,121,868 bytes, saved at `result/client-side/account.ui.com/_app/javascript/index-D5t7M7xo.js`.
- 39 routes + catch-all `*` inventoried in `result/inventory/routes.md`; 21 tested prior to this session.
- 0 confirmed vulnerabilities. Candidates: `CAND-001` (suspicious-login auto-confirm requires valid `confirm_token`), `CAND-002` (Zendesk `html_body` via `html-react-parser`, no sanitizer; blocked/no delivery).
- Redirect allowlist `MC`: `new URL(e).hostname.split('.').slice(-2).join('.')` must be in `['ubnt.com','ui.com','uisp.com']` and protocol `http:`/`https:` — verified no bypass.
- Zendesk ticket `create` body: `{ticket_form_id, requester, tags, subject, comment:{body}, custom_fields}` and no captcha header; `createComment`/`search` require `x-captcha-token`. Decision: do NOT create a test ticket — external side effect, and resulting HTML render would be self-XSS only (not reportable).
- Test data created then cleaned up: A/B addresses deleted (remaining `{"addresses":[]}`). Persistent side effect: A's beta roles were added by the authorized self opt-in endpoint.

